[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m **Step 1: Expected value of a single roll of an eight-sided die.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m An eight-sided die has faces numbered from 1 to 8. The expected value \(E(X)\) of a single roll is the average of these numbers. The formula for the expected value of a discrete uniform distribution is the average of the numbers from 1 to 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[
