[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m First, we convert the given rotations per minute into rotations per second:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m - The first gear turns \(33\frac{1}{3}\) times per minute. Since \(33\frac{1}{3} = \frac{100}{3}\), the gear turns \(\frac{100}{3}\) times per minute. Therefore, the gear turns \(\frac{100}{3} \times \frac{1}{60} = \frac{100}{180} = \frac{5}{9}\) times per second.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m - The second gear turns 45 times per minute. Therefore, the gear turns \(45 \times \frac{1}{60} = \frac{45}{60} = \frac{3}{4}\) times per second.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Next, we find the least common multiple of the fractions \(\frac{5}{9}\) and \(\frac{3}{4}\). To do this, we find the least common multiple of the denominators 9 and 4, which is 36. We then convert the fractions to have this common denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m - \(\frac{5}{9} = \frac{5 \times 4}{9 \times 4} = \frac{20}{36}\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m - \(\frac{3}{4} = \frac{3 \times 9}{4 \times 9} = \frac{27}{36}\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
