[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Here, \(a = 4\), \(b = 7\), and \(c = k\). The roots are \(\frac{-7 + i\sqrt{15}}{8}\) and \(\frac{-7 - i\sqrt{15}}{8}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m First, let's find the sum of the roots:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \text{Sum of the roots} = \frac{-7 + i\sqrt{15}}{8} + \frac{-7 - i\sqrt{15}}{8} = \frac{-7 + i\sqrt{15} - 7 - i\sqrt{15}}{8} = \frac{-14}{8} = -\frac{7}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m According to the sum of the roots formula, this should be equal to \(-\frac{b}{a} = -\frac{7}{4}\), which is consistent.
