[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m The formula for the volume of a cylinder is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m The formula for the volume of a sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m where \( r \) is the radius.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m - The height of the cylindrical beaker, \( h = 8 \) cm.
