[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m First, we need to find the velocity vector. The velocity vector is the derivative of the position vector with respect to time \(t\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m The position vector is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \mathbf{r}(t) = \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Taking the derivative of each component with respect to \(t\), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \mathbf{v}(t) = \left( \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right), \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Using the chain rule, we find:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[
