[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    The expected value \(E(X)\) of a single roll of an eight-sided die is the average of all possible outcomes. Since the die is fair, each face (1 through 8) has an equal probability of \(\frac{1}{8}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    The expected value is calculated as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    E(X) = \frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7 + 8}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    Summing the numbers from 1 to 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m    \[
