[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m [response] To determine the number of vertical asymptotes of the function \( y = \frac{2}{x^2 + x - 6} \), we need to identify the values of \( x \) that make the denominator zero, as these are the points where the function could have vertical asymptotes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m First, we factor the quadratic expression in the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ x^2 + x - 6 = (x + 3)(x - 2). \]
