[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ y = \frac{2}{(x + 3)(x - 2)}. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m The vertical asymptotes occur where the denominator is zero, provided the numerator is not zero at those points. Here, the denominator is zero when:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ x + 3 = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad x - 2 = 0. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m This gives us:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[ x = -3 \quad \text{or} \quad x = 2. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Since the numerator is a constant (2), it is never zero. Therefore, the function has vertical asymptotes at \( x = -3 \) and \( x = 2 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
