[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m The second and third inequalities are always satisfied for any positive \( x \) because \( 8 + x \) is always greater than 8. Therefore, the only relevant inequality is \( x < 16 \). Since \( x \) must be a whole number, the largest possible value for \( x \) is 15.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
