[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m a + b + c + d + e &= 8, \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 + e^2 &= 16.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m We want to maximize $e$. To do this, we can express $a + b + c + d$ in terms of $e$ from the first equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m a + b + c + d = 8 - e.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Next, we can use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality on the second equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m (a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2)(1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2) &\geq (a + b + c + d)^2, \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 4(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2) &\geq (8 - e)^2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Substituting $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 = 16 - e^2$ into the inequality, we get:
