[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Since the square root function is non-negative, we can square both sides to remove the square roots:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[5 | x | + 8 = x^2 - 16.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Rearranging the terms, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[x^2 - 5 | x | - 24 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m We can split this into two cases based on the definition of absolute value:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m **Case 1:** \(x \geq 0\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[x^2 - 5x - 24 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m Factoring the quadratic equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m \[(x - 8)(x + 3) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88572)[0m 
